# Wiki Documentation Required

**Plugin mode only.** Skip when the task is only gameplay YAML under `Ms_Scripts` / `MagicSpells_Scripting` (script mode) — pack content does not get wiki feature pages.

Any user-facing **plugin** spell, effect, or configuration change is incomplete until **`MagicSpells.wiki/`** is updated. Do this in the same task as the code change; do not leave wiki work as a follow-up unless the user explicitly defers it.

Conventions live in `MagicSpells.wiki/Wiki-Conventions.md` (page shape, shared-options callout, deprecation banners, redirects).

## When you must update the wiki

- **New spell** — new `*Spell.java` under `spells/`
- **New spell effect** — new type under `spelleffects/`
- **New or changed config options** — keys read via `getConfig*` / `getConfigData*` on spells, effects, or global YAML (`general.yml`, `mana.yml`, modifiers, variables, magic items, etc.)
- **Behavior changes that affect how configs are written** — defaults, formats, removed options, renamed keys
- **New modifier condition** — `Modifier-Condition-List.md` + `Modifiers.md`
- **Removed / replaced type** — deprecation banner on the old page; prefer redirect stub over deleting

Skip wiki edits only for pure internals (refactors with no YAML/API surface change).

## What to create or edit

1. **Feature page** in `MagicSpells.wiki/` (match nearby naming; prefer `ClassName.md` / `Title-With-Hyphens.md` consistent with siblings).
2. **Index entry**:
   - Spells → `Spell-List.md` (correct category: general / command / instant / targeted / buff). Format each bullet as link + `` (`spell-class`) `` + em-dash one-liner of purpose; do not add a bare name-only link.
   - Effects → `Spell-Effects.md` (one-liner per `effect:` type)
   - Modifier conditions → `Modifier-Condition-List.md` (and detail on `Modifiers.md`)
   - Global options → `General-Configuration.md`, `Mana-Configuration.md`, `Modifiers.md`, `Variables.md`, etc.
3. After spell/option/effect/modifier doc changes that affect inventories, regenerate from the workspace root: `python3 scripts/wiki/generate-all.py` (writes `spell-index.json`, `effect-index.json`, `modifier-condition-index.json`, `configdata-coverage.md`, etc. into `MagicSpells.wiki/`). CI runs the same checks.
4. **Sidebar** (`_Sidebar.md`) only if adding a top-level doc category, not for every spell page.

## Page shape (mirror strong examples)

Use pages like `ConjureSpell.md` or `DummySpell.md` as templates:

- Link to source on this fork, e.g.  
  `https://github.com/Team-Sneakymouse/MagicSpells/blob/DvZ/core/src/main/java/.../YourSpell.java`
- Show `spell-class` (e.g. `.instant.YourSpell`) or effect `effect:` name
- Short **Description**
- Shared-options callout:  
  `> **Shared options:** [[Spell Configuration]]. This page lists only options this type owns.`  
  (Buffs: also link [[Buff Spell]].)
- **Configuration** table: Option | Description | Default Value | ConfigData (add Type when peers do). **ConfigData** is `yes` if the Java field is loaded via `getConfigData*` / `ConfigDataUtil` (expression-capable at cast time), else `no`. Do not invent ConfigData support in code just to flip the cell — report current behavior only.
- At least one minimal YAML example
- Document only options this type owns; link [[Spell Configuration]] / [[Spell Effects]] for shared base options
- Every owned config key from the Java constructor/`load` path must appear in the table; if you find an undocumented key, add it

## Quality bar

- Defaults and key names must match the Java/YAML source exactly.
- If you remove or rename a config key in code, update or strike it on the wiki in the same change.
- Wiki is its own git repo — stage/commit there separately from `MagicSpells/` when the user asks for commits.
